[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    - A number \( n \) has exactly three distinct positive divisors if and only if it is the square of a prime number. This is because the divisors of \( p^2 \) (where \( p \) is a prime) are \( 1, p, \) and \( p^2 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 2. **Identifying the Primes**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    - We need to find all prime numbers \( p \) such that \( p^2 < 1000 \).
