[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    I = 40 \text{ amperes}, \quad R = 3 \text{ ohms}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    Using Ohm's law \( V = IR \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    V = 40 \times 3 = 120 \text{ volts}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 2. **Find the current \( I \) when the resistance \( R \) is 20 ohms, assuming the voltage \( V \) remains constant:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    Given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    V = 120 \text{ volts}, \quad R = 20 \text{ ohms}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    Using Ohm's law \( V = IR \) and solving for \( I \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    \[
