[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 1. **Identify the Midpoints and Parallel Lines:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    - Since \(E\) and \(F\) are midpoints, \(EF\) is parallel to both \(AB\) and \(DC\) and is the midsegment of the trapezoid. This means \(EF = \frac{1}{2}(AB + DC)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 2. **Area Relationships:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    - Let the area of trapezoid \(ABCD\) be \(A\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    - The area of \(ABEF\) is twice the area of \(FECD\). Let the area of \(FECD\) be \(x\). Then the area of \(ABEF\) is \(2x\).
