[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m [response] To solve this problem, we need to calculate the volume of the cylindrical beaker and the volume of the spherical tank, and then determine how many beakers are needed to fill the tank.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m ### Step 1: Calculate the volume of the cylindrical beaker
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m The formula for the volume of a cylinder is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ V_{\text{cylinder}} = \pi r^2 h \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m where \( r \) is the radius and \( h \) is the height.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m - Radius \( r = 3 \) cm
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m - Height \( h = 8 \) cm
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Substitute the values into the formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ V_{\text{cylinder}} = \pi (3)^2 (8) = \pi \cdot 9 \cdot 8 = 72\pi \, \text{cm}^3 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m ### Step 2: Calculate the volume of the spherical tank
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m The formula for the volume of a sphere is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ V_{\text{sphere}} = \frac{4}{3} \pi r^3 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m where \( r \) is the radius.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m - Radius \( r = 6 \) cm
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Substitute the values into the formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ V_{\text{sphere}} = \frac{4}{3} \pi (6)^3 = \frac{4}{3} \pi \cdot 216 = 288\pi \, \text{cm}^3 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m ### Step 3: Determine how many beakers are needed to fill the tank
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m To find out how many beakers are needed, we divide the volume of the spherical tank by the volume of one cylindrical beaker:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ \text{Number of beakers} = \frac{V_{\text{sphere}}}{V_{\text{cylinder}}} = \frac{288\pi}{72\pi} = \frac{288}{72} = 4 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Therefore, it will take 4 cylindrical beakers to fill the spherical tank.
