[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m - The mass of the softball (\(m_{\text{softball}}\)) is 200 g.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m - The mass of the baseball (\(m_{\text{baseball}}\)) is 150 g.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m - The force applied by Jen (\(F_{\text{Jen}}\)) is the same as the force applied by Jack (\(F_{\text{Jack}}\)).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m We need to find the ratio of the acceleration of Jen's ball to Jack's ball, which is \(\frac{a_{\text{Jen}}}{a_{\text{Jack}}}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m From the formula \(F = ma\), we can express the acceleration as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ a = \frac{F}{m} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Since the force is the same for both balls, we can write:
