[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m ### Saturday's Delivery Route
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Eli starts at \(z\) and travels to \(z^3, z^5, \ldots, z^{2013}\). The last house he visits is at \(z^{2013}\). The distance from \(z\) to \(z^{2013}\) is given as \(\sqrt{2012}\). This means:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[|z^{2013} - z| = \sqrt{2012}\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m ### Sunday's Delivery Route
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Eli starts at \(1\) and travels to \(z^2, z^4, \ldots, z^{2012}\). The last house he visits is at \(z^{2012}\). The distance from \(1\) to \(z^{2012}\) is also given as \(\sqrt{2012}\). This means:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[|z^{2012} - 1| = \sqrt{2012}\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m ### Analyzing the Magnitudes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Since \(|z^{2013} - z| = \sqrt{2012}\) and \(|z^{2012} - 1| = \sqrt{2012}\), we can infer that the magnitudes of \(z^{2013}\) and \(z^{2012}\) are such that the distances from \(z\) and \(1\) respectively are \(\sqrt{2012}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m ### Considering the Angle
