[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m To minimize $D^2$, we take the derivative with respect to $x$ and set it to zero:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[\frac{d}{dx}(x^4 - 9x^2 + 25) = 4x^3 - 18x = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Factoring out $2x$, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[2x(2x^2 - 9) = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m This gives us $x = 0$ or $x = \pm\sqrt{\frac{9}{2}} = \pm\frac{3\sqrt{2}}{2}$. 
