[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ x(t) = 3 \sin \frac{t}{4} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ y(t) = 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Differentiating \(x(t)\) and \(y(t)\) with respect to \(t\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ \frac{dx}{dt} = 3 \cdot \frac{1}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4} = \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ \frac{dy}{dt} = 3 \cdot \left(-\frac{1}{4}\right) \sin \frac{t}{4} = -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m The speed of the particle is the magnitude of the velocity vector, which is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ \text{Speed} = \sqrt{\left(\frac{dx}{dt}\right)^2 + \left(\frac{dy}{dt}\right)^2} = \sqrt{\left(\frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4}\right)^2 + \left(-\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4}\right)^2} \]
