[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m Now, we use the same voltage to find the current when the resistance is \(20 \text{ \(\Omega\)}\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ V = IR \implies 120 \text{ V} = I \times 20 \text{ \(\Omega\)} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m \[ I = \frac{120 \text{ V}}{20 \text{ \(\Omega\)}} = 6 \text{ A} \]
