[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m [response] To solve this problem, we need to calculate the volume of the cylindrical beaker and the volume of the spherical tank, and then determine how many beakers are needed to fill the tank.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 1. **Volume of the cylindrical beaker:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    The formula for the volume of a cylinder is \( V = \pi r^2 h \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    Here, \( r = 3 \) cm and \( h = 8 \) cm.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    V_{\text{cylinder}} = \pi \times 3^2 \times 8 = 72\pi \text{ cm}^3
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m 2. **Volume of the spherical tank:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1412833)[0m    The formula for the volume of a sphere is \( V = \frac{4}{3} \pi r^3 \).
